// Post-Quantum (ML-DSA) hardfork — enables pq_key_auths, pq_signatures,
// witness_pq_signature, and pq_serialization_active committee param.
// Placeholder date — the real value is set by the committee when the
// feature is scheduled for a particular network.
//
// SIZING NOTE (verified on a devnet, see below for what does NOT apply):
// An ML-DSA-65 public key is 1952 bytes and a signature is 3309 bytes.
// PQ *signatures* do NOT count against `maximum_transaction_size`: that check
// uses transaction::get_packed_size(), which packs only the transaction body
// (ref_block_num, ref_block_prefix, expiration, operations, extensions) and
// excludes both classical and PQ signatures. A PQ-signed transfer carrying a
// 5261-byte signature was accepted on a devnet with maximum_transaction_size
// set to 4096.
// What DOES count is any operation that embeds a PQ public key: each key adds
// 1952 bytes to the operation body. migrate_wallet installs one in both the
// active and the owner authority, so an account_update from it runs ~3.9 KB
// and does not fit the historical 2048 default -- which is why
// libraries/egenesis/genesis-pq.json raises maximum_transaction_size to 4096.
// A chain enabling pq_serialization_active should make sure its own
// `maximum_transaction_size` leaves room for these key-bearing operations.
#ifndef HARDFORK_PQ_0_TIME
#define HARDFORK_PQ_0_TIME                        (fc::time_point_sec( 1893456000 ))
#define HARDFORK_PQ_0_PASSED(head_block_time)     (head_block_time >= HARDFORK_PQ_0_TIME)
#endif
